body:
A difference from the existing warning ignore system (`ScriptTextEditor::_warning_clicked`) is that this always adds a new `@warning_ignore()` line, but before it tried to detect if there was already a warning ignore and add the warning to the list.
```gdscript
func test_unsafe_void_return() -> void:
	# using warning panel:
	#@warning_ignore("unsafe_method_access", "unsafe_void_return")
	# using code actions:
	@warning_ignore("unsafe_method_access")
	@warning_ignore("unsafe_void_return")
	return variant_func().f()
```

It would be nice if this could do the same and add to a previous `warning_ignore`.

(In the future the current warning panel ignore system should be replaced with this)

