body:
I have most of this implemented now: using the shortcut places the menu at the caret position (including column), and when clicking the button it instead finds its position based on the button's position.

I've run into a difficult situation with preventing the top-left-corner-popup problem. In VS Code, I see that the editor simply moves the viewport such that the caret is visible again, and then places the popup at the now-visible caret. I tried to do the same thing here:

```cpp
Rect2 line_rect;
int l = text_editor->get_caret_line();
int c = text_editor->get_caret_column();

if (!text_editor->is_caret_visible()) {
	text_editor->adjust_viewport_to_caret();
}
line_rect = text_editor->get_rect_at_line_column(l, c);
```
The viewport shifts to make the caret visible, as expected, but the popup still appears at the top-left corner. I'm fairly sure this is because the data that TextEdit uses for `get_rect_at_line_column()` isn't updated until the frame/redraw following `adjust_viewport_to_caret()`. 

Does this sound like a likely cause to you? If so, do you know if there's an easy way to force it to recalculate those values? If not, I may be able to move that code into a dedicated function and call it from `adjust_viewport_to_caret()` so that it's immediately available, but first I'd like to ensure there's not a more straightforward solution I'm missing 😅

Edit: Looking closer at the `NOTIFICATION_DRAW` code for TextEdit, I'm not quite as sure now that it'd be possible/feasible to extract the code for recalculating the rect information...

